data.content:
**In .NET 11, all synchronous I/O on the EF Core Cosmos DB provider is permanently removed — no opt-in exists anymore.**

In .NET 10 you could re-enable sync-over-async with a configuration flag. In EF Core 11, calling any sync API (`ToList()`, `First()`, `Count()`, `SaveChanges()`) **always throws** at runtime. There is no workaround.

**Fix — convert everything to async:**

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

All callers up the chain must be updated to `await` these methods. The `Add()` call itself is fine — it's an in-memory operation — but `SaveChanges()` must become `SaveChangesAsync()`.

Tracking issue: [dotnet/efcore#37059](https://github.com/dotnet/efcore/issues/37059)
